  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "lB039l8R2AnpBSMJda/WXVFloZo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:26:27.021Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "This group is a negative finding recorded where a demo design would normally sit. Mendix occupies the app-layer slot, so there is no complementary integration to build \u2014 the research text rules the complement framing out explicitly. What remains is a migration story: one app rebuilt as a typed spec, shown as a substitution rather than an addition.\n\nThe targeting is as specific as the mechanism. The migration is aimed at deals too small to justify a seat, which moves the argument off capability and onto licence economics. That is a narrow wedge, and it is the only one this cohort supports.\n\nThe six leads are all Dutch and all deeply committed to the platform per their source rows \u2014 Benelux Partner of the Year, Mendix EXPERT, a dedicated low-code operating company, and combinations with SAP, Siemens PLM, OutSystems and Dynamics. Four are marked \"2 \u00b7 decide thesis first\" and two \"9 \u00b7 do not pitch\", so the corpus itself records that the displacement thesis is unresolved. The decision to be made is upstream of any pitch: whether Powerhouse competes for the app layer at all.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (6)\n\n**2 \u00b7 decide thesis first**\n- Blue Green Solutions (NL \u00b7 not verified)\n- CAPE (NL \u00b7 not verified)\n- Emixa (NL \u00b7 530+)\n- Finaps (NL \u00b7 not verified)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- CLEVR (NL \u00b7 250+)\n- Conclusion (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> NOT a complement \u2014 Mendix occupies the app-layer slot. Migration story only: one app rebuilt as a typed spec, aimed at deals too small to justify a seat.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:26:27.021500Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:26:27.021505Z"
    }
  },
